Note body touch-mode controls minimap positioning; set only in hunt/camp, good.

Need showResult maybe world hud hide handled in game.

Check `showPause` maybe hide world? no.

Now styles append. We need account mobile touch. Write comprehensive CSS at end.

Design positions:

```
/* world hud */
#world-ui{z-index:4}
.minimap-wrap{position:absolute;left:calc(18px+safe-l);bottom:calc(18px+safe-b);width:138px;height:160px;pointer-events:none}
#minimap{width:138px;height:138px;border-radius:50%;display:block;filter:drop-shadow...}
.minimap-clock{... height 18 ...}
.map-open-btn{position:absolute;right:-2px;top:2px;pointer-events:auto;...}
.camp-menu-btn{position:absolute;top:calc(16px+safe-top);left:calc(18px+safe-l);pointer-events:auto;...}
.interact-prompt{position:absolute;left:50%;bottom:calc(196px+safe-b);transform...;pointer-events:auto;display:flex...}
```
Note `.hidden{display:none!important}` will hide interact. Good.

In hunt, `.hud-player` top-left; minimap bottom-left. Good.
In camp, camp-menu top-left; no player bars; okay.
In hub, camp menu hidden; map visible bottom-left.

Minimap wrap height 160; item readout bottom 168, okay. But `.subtitle` bottom 138 might overlap minimap horizontally left center? subtitle centered, width up to 80vw; could overlap bottom-left. Minimap 138 from left, subtitle likely center; not too bad. On mobile reposition.

